                                "sense_id": "7d9d9981-f0f4-3709-9ff3-35c3966530d3",
                                "text": "About ten A.M. another camalote of very large size, apparently two acres in extent, floated into the midst of us. […] There islands are sometimes very compact, and capable of sustaining a considerable weight. There is a well-authenticated story of two tigers being drifted down upon a camalote as far as Monte Video, where the beasts created great alam."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "555200f1-5c2f-4e9f-8836-6b5d95756cda",
                                "sense_id": "7d9d9981-f0f4-3709-9ff3-35c3966530d3",
                                "text": "A camalote is a floating island of river plants often with enough root structure to support one or more men. Later in the war, the Paraguayans camou- flaged canoes as camalotes so as to approach the Brazilian fleet undetected."
